==Trivia==
*The word "''Bandit''" comes from the Latin "''bannio''", meaning 'to ban'.
**In the French and Korean language settings of the game, the Bandit's name translates to "Thief". In the Italian, Dutch, Japanese, Chinese, Finnish, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Bandit's name translates to "Outlaw", "Highwaywoman", "Assassin", "Phantom Assassin", "Robber", and "Pirate" respectively.
**The Bandit is 1 of 4 [[cards]] associated with outlawry, with the others being [[Goblin Gang]], [[Rascals]], and the [[Boss Bandit]].
**Along with the [[Firecracker]], Rascals, [[Magic Archer]], and the Boss Bandit, the Bandit belongs to the Forest Gang.
*The Bandit is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], Rascals, [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], Magic Archer, [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Bandit is 1 of 23 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons|Skeleton Dragons,]] [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], Firecracker, Rascal Girls, Royal Hogs, [[Heal Spirit]], Elixir Golem, [[Guards]], Prince, Balloon, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Ram Rider, [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], Royal Ghost, [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
*In the Japanese language setting of the game, the Bandit's personal name is revealed to be "''Juno''".
*The Bandit will whistle before dashing and often says “''Ha!''” when attacking.
*If the Boss Bandit takes down an opposing Bandit, she may say "''This is why I'm the boss!''". If the Boss Bandit is taken down by an opposing Bandit, she may say "''Beaten by you?''". If the Boss Bandit is played when an allied Bandit is on the field, she may say "''Bandit, watch and learn!''".
*The Bandit is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
*When 2 Bandits face each other, they will charge at each other, but neither side would be damaged by the other's dash. In a one-on-one duel between them, the Bandit that was placed second will survive, instead of both being defeated at the same time.
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Bandit does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*In the Chinese language setting of the game, the card description incorrectly mentions that the Bandit does double damage with her dash, as at some Levels, she deals 1 more than double.
*The Bandit was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/DVY2TndGf4U?si=ptuVz0tHkkkDIvEl Crown Championship Global Series Tournament], by a player called Sergioramos:).
*On 27/3/2023, a [[Training Camp|Trainer]] was added to the game called Boss Cheddar, and used a Level 18 Bandit in their deck, despite the highest Level being Level 14 at the time. This Trainer was removed on 18/4/2023.
*The original concept of the Bandit was the Royal Ghost, with an invisibility and dash mechanic, along with a stun. However, the stun mechanic was dropped, and the dash mechanic lead to the creation of the Bandit. Ultimately, the Royal Ghost was added in one of Clash Royale's updates.
*The 17/3/2017 Bandit Draft Challenge was originally going to reward players with 100 [[Gems]] after reaching 2 victories. However, this was changed to a Golden [[Chests|Chest]] [https://www.reddit.com/r/ClashRoyale/comments/5zio9d/bandit_draft_challenge_entry_cost_reward_changes/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x&context=3 last minute]. It was also changed to have a free first entry fee instead of a 100 Gem entry free.

